(DOSAMATIC and CP/M emulator).  It is amusing to run 'strings' over
the .com files and examine the copyright notices and 'You shouldn't be
poking around in here' messages.  In all fairness, the CP/M appears to
be clean (it's shareware), and I haven't examined DOSAMATIC in enough
detail, though I suspect it's shareware as well.  Imagine if someone
posted a copy of LOTUS 1-2-3 with shareware notices in it.  No more
net.sources, maybe even no more USENET.

